.TH AD_LAYER_OVERWRITE 1 "2026-08-30" "ad 2.0" "ad layers"
.SH NAME
ad_layer_overwrite \- merge delete+insert pairs into overwrite_insert ops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_layer_overwrite
< post_ops > overwrite_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_layer_overwrite
detects adjacent delete+insert pairs at the same (line, col) and merges them into a single
.B overwrite_insert
op. This produces a more natural "in-place replacement" visual instead of "delete all, then insert all".
.PP
A pair is merged when:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
op[i] is a non-newline DELETE
.IP \(bu 3
op[i+1] is a non-newline INSERT
.IP \(bu 3
Both have the same (line, col)
.IP \(bu 3
The previous op was NOT a delete at the same position (pd flag)
.IP \(bu 3
The op after next is NOT an insert at the same line (ni flag)
.RE
.PP
After merging, positions are recomputed by walking the output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to /tmp/ad_debug/.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
V2 TSV format. Input should be post-reorder (see
.BR ad_layer_reorder (1)).
.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. This layer has no user-configurable options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_layer_overwrite < reordered_ops.txt > overwrite_ops.txt
Merge delete+insert pairs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_layer_reorder (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
